IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 104.1 to 107 -- INFORMATION, AGREEMENTS AND OATHS.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2731 to 2777 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 104.1 lets information obtained for the administration of the Act pass between named federal departments, and stops it
-- passing further except for the same purpose and on the conditions the Minister specifies. Section 105 lets the Minister agree
-- with a province providing a comprehensive pension plan to exchange information and to let the province's authority give a
-- contributor a statement of the Record of Earnings. Section 106 makes certain employees commissioners for oaths for the Act's
-- purposes. Section 107 lets the Minister agree with a foreign government on reciprocal arrangements (subsection 107(3) is a
-- regulation-making power: inert, NOTES.md).
--
-- WHAT A PERSON IS EXPOSED TO. These provisions are written for officials; the person's side is the liability they create:
-- information about a contributor may be passed from one department to another "despite any other Act or law" (s 104.1(1)), may
-- go no further unless for the same purpose and on the Minister's conditions (s 104.1(2)), may go to a province's authority under
-- an agreement (s 105(a)), and a contributor may be given the statement of the Record by that authority instead of the Minister (s 105(b)).
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS (NOTES.md has the table): the public officer's liberty to share and the contributor's no-right to confidentiality
-- (s 104.1(1)); the public officer's duty not to share further and the contributor's claim (s 104.1(2)); the Minister's power to agree and
-- the government's liability to be agreed with (ss 105, 107); the authorized person's power to take oaths and the deponent's liability
-- to have an oath taken (s 106).
--
-- Out of range, taken as inputs: the Financial Administration Act Schedules (s 106(2)), prescribed conditions (s 105(a); no Regulation
-- among the inputs prescribes them), and the terms of any agreement (not among the texts this encoding reads).
-- NOTHING means that another instrument governs the case and is not among the texts this encoding reads.

§ `Part III -- information, agreements with provinces and countries, and oaths (sections 104.1 to 107)`

§§ `Section 104.1 -- availability of information within federal institutions`

-- The six bodies the section names, and a member for every other body.
-- src:2740 | Availability of information within federal institutions
-- src:2741 | 104.1 (1) Despite any other Act or law, any information obtained by a public officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, the Department of Finance, the Department of Public Works and Government Services or the Department of Citizenship and Immigration for the purpose of the administration of this Act may be made available to a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development, the Canada Revenue Agency, the Department of Finance, the Department of Public Works and Government Services, the Department of Citizenship and Immigration or the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions for the purpose of the administration of this Act.
@ref Act s 104.1(1) (src:2740-2741)
DECLARE `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1` IS ONE OF
    `the Canada Revenue Agency`
    `the Department of Finance`
    `the Department of Public Works and Government Services`
    `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration`
    `the Department of Employment and Social Development`
    `the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions`
    `another body`

-- "obtained by a public officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, the Department of Finance, the Department of Public Works and
-- Government Services or the Department of Citizenship and Immigration".
@ref Act s 104.1(1) (src:2741)
GIVEN body IS A `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `the Canada Revenue Agency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Finance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Public Works and Government Services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Employment and Social Development` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another body` THEN FALSE

-- "may be made available to a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development, the Canada Revenue Agency,
-- the Department of Finance, the Department of Public Works and Government Services, the Department of Citizenship and
-- Immigration or the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions".
@ref Act s 104.1(1) (src:2741)
GIVEN body IS A `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `the Canada Revenue Agency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Finance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Public Works and Government Services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Citizenship and Immigration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Department of Employment and Social Development` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another body` THEN FALSE

-- Whether the two are public officers is section 104(1) "public officer" (cp6-interpretation.l4); here each is a yes/no input.
@ref Act s 104.1(1) (src:2741)
GIVEN `the holder of the information` IS A `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1`
      `the holder is a public officer of that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was obtained for the purpose of the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient` IS A `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1`
      `the recipient is a public officer of that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is made available for the purpose of the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law` `the holder of the information` `the holder is a public officer of that body` `the information was obtained for the purpose of the administration of this Act` `the recipient` `the recipient is a public officer of that body` `the information is made available for the purpose of the administration of this Act` MEANS
        `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may make the information available` `the holder of the information`
    AND `the holder is a public officer of that body`
    AND `the information was obtained for the purpose of the administration of this Act`
    AND `s 104.1(1) — the body is one whose public officer may be given the information` `the recipient`
    AND `the recipient is a public officer of that body`
    AND `the information is made available for the purpose of the administration of this Act`

-- "shall not be made available to any other person or body unless ...": the subsection governs a person or body that is not a
-- public officer of a body in subsection (1); onward passing among those officers is subsection (1)'s (fork C6-F13).
-- NOTHING: the subsection does not govern the case.
-- src:2742 | Secondary release of information
-- src:2743 | (2) Information obtained under this section shall not be made available to any other person or body unless the information is made available only for the same purpose and on any conditions that the Minister may specify.
@ref Act s 104.1(2) (src:2742-2743)
GIVEN `the information was obtained under section 104.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is a person or body other than a public officer of a body named in subsection 104.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is made available only for the same purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is made available on any conditions the Minister specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` `the information was obtained under section 104.1` `the recipient is a person or body other than a public officer of a body named in subsection 104.1(1)` `the information is made available only for the same purpose` `the information is made available on any conditions the Minister specifies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the information was obtained under section 104.1` AND `the recipient is a person or body other than a public officer of a body named in subsection 104.1(1)`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the information is made available only for the same purpose` AND `the information is made available on any conditions the Minister specifies`)

-- Sections 104.01 to 104.09, 104.101, 104.102 and 104.11 (lines 2731 to 2739 and 2744 to 2746) are repealed in this text and state nothing.

§§ `Section 105 -- agreement with a province for exchange of records`

-- src:2748 | Agreements with Provinces
-- src:2749 | Agreement with province for exchange of records and furnishing of information
-- src:2750 | 105 The Minister may, on behalf of the Government of Canada, enter into an agreement with the government of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan
@ref Act s 105 (src:2748-2750)
GIVEN province IS A Province
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105 — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province about records and information` province MEANS
    province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`

-- src:2751 | (a) under which any information obtained under this Act, including records of any amounts that are shown in the Record of Earnings to the accounts of individuals who have made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan of that province and that relate to the contributions made by those individuals under this Act, may be made available under prescribed conditions to the appropriate authority of that province having the administration of the provincial pension plan, and under which any information obtained under the provincial pension plan may be made available on a reciprocal basis to the Minister; and
DECLARE `cp6 Direction in which an agreement under section 105 lets information go` IS ONE OF
    `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province`
    `from the appropriate authority of the province to the Minister`

@ref Act s 105(a) (src:2751)
GIVEN direction IS A `cp6 Direction in which an agreement under section 105 lets information go`
      `the agreement is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was obtained under the plan of the party that holds it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is made available under prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is made available on a reciprocal basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` direction `the agreement is in force` `the information was obtained under the plan of the party that holds it` `the information is made available under prescribed conditions` `the information is made available on a reciprocal basis` MEANS
        `the agreement is in force`
    AND `the information was obtained under the plan of the party that holds it`
    AND CONSIDER direction
        -- information obtained under this Act: "may be made available under prescribed conditions to the appropriate authority of that province"
        WHEN `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province` THEN `the information is made available under prescribed conditions`
        -- information obtained under the provincial plan: "may be made available on a reciprocal basis to the Minister"
        WHEN `from the appropriate authority of the province to the Minister` THEN `the information is made available on a reciprocal basis`

-- src:2752 | (b) under which the Minister or the appropriate authority of that province, in accordance with any terms and conditions that may be specified in the agreement, may make available to any individual who has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan a statement of any amounts shown in the Record of Earnings or the appropriate records established under the provincial pension plan, as the case may be, to the account of that individual, and may act on or give effect to any request made by that individual for reconsideration by the Minister or the appropriate authority, as the case may be, of any statement made available to the individual.
@ref Act s 105(b) (src:2752)
GIVEN `the agreement is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions the agreement specifies are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105(b) — a statement of the amounts shown to the individual's account may be made available by the Minister or the provincial authority` `the agreement is in force` `the individual has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan` `the terms and conditions the agreement specifies are met` MEANS
        `the agreement is in force`
    AND `the individual has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan`
    AND `the terms and conditions the agreement specifies are met`

@ref Act s 105(b) (src:2752)
GIVEN `the agreement is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions the agreement specifies are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has made a request for reconsideration of a statement made available to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105(b) — the Minister or the provincial authority may act on the individual's request for reconsideration` `the agreement is in force` `the individual has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan` `the terms and conditions the agreement specifies are met` `the individual has made a request for reconsideration of a statement made available to the individual` MEANS
        `the agreement is in force`
    AND `the individual has made contributions under this Act and under the provincial pension plan`
    AND `the terms and conditions the agreement specifies are met`
    AND `the individual has made a request for reconsideration of a statement made available to the individual`

§§ `Section 106 -- oaths, affidavits, declarations and affirmations`

-- src:2754 | Oaths, Affidavits, Declarations and Affirmations
-- src:2755 | Commissioners for oaths
-- src:2756 | 106 (1) A person who
-- src:2757 | (a) is employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or any regulations made thereunder and is authorized by the Minister of National Revenue for the purpose, or
-- src:2758 | (b) is employed in the administration or enforcement of this Part and Part II or any regulations made thereunder and is authorized by the Minister for the purpose,
-- src:2759 | may, in the course of their employment and subject to any other Act of Parliament or any Act of the legislature of a province, administer oaths and take and receive affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations and every person so authorized has, with respect to any such oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation, all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits.
DECLARE `cp6 Employee authorized to take oaths for the Act` IS ONE OF
    `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue`
    `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister`
    `neither of those`

-- NOTHING: "subject to any other Act of Parliament or any Act of the legislature of a province", which is not read here.
@ref Act s 106(1) (src:2754-2759)
GIVEN employee IS A `cp6 Employee authorized to take oaths for the Act`
      `the person acts in the course of their employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act of Parliament or an Act of a legislature of a province limits the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` employee `the person acts in the course of their employment` `another Act of Parliament or an Act of a legislature of a province limits the power` MEANS
    IF `another Act of Parliament or an Act of a legislature of a province limits the power`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `the person acts in the course of their employment`
               AND CONSIDER employee
                   WHEN `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` THEN TRUE
                   WHEN `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister` THEN TRUE
                   WHEN `neither of those` THEN FALSE)

-- src:2760 | Acceptance of oaths, etc.
-- src:2761 | (2) For the purposes of the administration of
-- src:2762 | (a) Part I or any regulations made under that Part, any person described in paragraph (1)(a), or
-- src:2763 | (b) this Part or Part II or any regulations made under either of those Parts, any person described in paragraph (1)(b)
-- src:2764 | may accept any oath administered or affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation given by any officer or employee of any department in, or other portion of, the federal public administration specified in Schedule I, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act or of any department of the government of a province who has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits.
@ref Act s 106(2) (src:2760-2764)
GIVEN acceptor IS A `cp6 Employee authorized to take oaths for the Act`
      `the oath, affidavit, declaration or affirmation is for the purposes of the Part or regulations that the acceptor's own paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker is an officer or employee of a department or other portion of the federal public administration specified in Schedule I, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act, or of a department of the government of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 106(2) — the authorized person may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` acceptor `the oath, affidavit, declaration or affirmation is for the purposes of the Part or regulations that the acceptor's own paragraph names` `the maker is an officer or employee of a department or other portion of the federal public administration specified in Schedule I, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act, or of a department of the government of a province` `the maker has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` MEANS
        CONSIDER acceptor
        WHEN `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `neither of those` THEN FALSE
    AND `the oath, affidavit, declaration or affirmation is for the purposes of the Part or regulations that the acceptor's own paragraph names`
    AND `the maker is an officer or employee of a department or other portion of the federal public administration specified in Schedule I, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act, or of a department of the government of a province`
    AND `the maker has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits`

§§ `Section 107 -- reciprocal agreements with other countries`

-- src:2766 | Reciprocal Agreements with Other Countries
-- src:2767 | Reciprocal arrangements re administration, etc.
-- src:2768 | 107 (1) Where, under any law of a country other than Canada, provision is made for the payment of old age or other benefits including survivors’ or disability benefits, the Minister may, on behalf of the Government of Canada, on such terms and conditions as may be approved by the Governor in Council, enter into an agreement with the government of that country for the making of reciprocal arrangements relating to the administration or operation of that law and of this Act, including, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, arrangements relating to
@ref Act s 107(1) (src:2766-2768)
GIVEN `a law of the other country makes provision for the payment of old age or other benefits, including survivors' or disability benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions are approved by the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country` `a law of the other country makes provision for the payment of old age or other benefits, including survivors' or disability benefits` `the terms and conditions are approved by the Governor in Council` MEANS
        `a law of the other country makes provision for the payment of old age or other benefits, including survivors' or disability benefits`
    AND `the terms and conditions are approved by the Governor in Council`

-- src:2769 | (a) the exchange of such information obtained under that law or this Act as may be necessary to give effect to any such arrangements,
-- src:2770 | (b) the administration of benefits payable under this Act to persons resident in that country, the extension of benefits to and in respect of persons under that law or this Act and the increase or decrease in the amount of the benefits payable under that law or this Act to and in respect of persons employed in or resident in that country, and
-- src:2771 | (c) the administration of benefits payable under that law to persons resident in Canada, the extension of benefits to and in respect of persons under that law or this Act and the increase or decrease in the amount of the benefits payable under that law or this Act to and in respect of persons employed in or resident in Canada,
-- src:2772 | and, subject to subsection (4), any such agreement may extend to and include similar arrangements with respect to any provincial pension plan.
DECLARE `cp6 Arrangement an agreement under subsection 107(1) may make` IS ONE OF
    `the exchange of information obtained under that law or this Act`
    `the administration of benefits payable under this Act to persons resident in that country, and their extension, increase or decrease`
    `the administration of benefits payable under that law to persons resident in Canada, and their extension, increase or decrease`
    `another arrangement relating to the administration or operation of that law and of this Act`
    `an arrangement that does not relate to the administration or operation of either`

-- "including, without restricting the generality of the foregoing": the three listed arrangements and every other arrangement
-- relating to the administration or operation of the two laws are within the subsection.
@ref Act s 107(1) (src:2769-2772)
GIVEN arrangement IS A `cp6 Arrangement an agreement under subsection 107(1) may make`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107(1) — the agreement may make the arrangement` arrangement MEANS
    CONSIDER arrangement
    WHEN `the exchange of information obtained under that law or this Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the administration of benefits payable under this Act to persons resident in that country, and their extension, increase or decrease` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the administration of benefits payable under that law to persons resident in Canada, and their extension, increase or decrease` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another arrangement relating to the administration or operation of that law and of this Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an arrangement that does not relate to the administration or operation of either` THEN FALSE

-- "and, subject to subsection (4), any such agreement may extend to and include similar arrangements with respect to any
-- provincial pension plan".
@ref Act s 107(1) (src:2769-2772)
GIVEN `the arrangement is about a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of subsection 107(4) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107(1) — the agreement may extend to a similar arrangement about a provincial pension plan` `the arrangement is about a provincial pension plan` `the conditions of subsection 107(4) are met` MEANS
    `the arrangement is about a provincial pension plan` AND `the conditions of subsection 107(4) are met`

-- Paragraphs (b) and (c): the agreement may deal with "the extension of benefits to and in respect of persons under that law or this Act and the
-- increase or decrease in the amount of the benefits payable under that law or this Act to and in respect of persons employed in or resident in" the
-- other country (b) or Canada (c). The Act says that an agreement MAY do this; whether it does, and by how much, is in the agreement, which is
-- not among the texts this encoding reads, so no amount is computed here.
@ref Act s 107(1)(b), (c) (src:2770-2771)
GIVEN `an agreement under subsection 107(1) is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed in or resident in the other country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed in or resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107(1)(b) and (c) — the agreement may provide for the benefits payable to or in respect of the person to be extended, increased or decreased` `an agreement under subsection 107(1) is in force` `the person is employed in or resident in the other country` `the person is employed in or resident in Canada` MEANS
        `an agreement under subsection 107(1) is in force`
    AND (`the person is employed in or resident in the other country` OR `the person is employed in or resident in Canada`)

-- Subsection 107(2) (line 2773) is repealed in this text. Subsection 107(3) (line 2775) is a regulation-making power: inert, NOTES.md.

-- src:2776 | Agreements with respect to provincial pension plan
-- src:2777 | (4) Where the government of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan requests the Government of Canada to enter into an agreement under this section with the government of a country under any law of which provision is made for the payment of old age or other benefits including survivors’ or disability benefits, the Minister, with the approval of the Governor in Council, may enter into an agreement with the government of that country for the making of reciprocal arrangements relating to any of the matters referred to in subsection (1) with respect to the provincial pension plan of that province, if that plan makes provision for entering into such an agreement and for the carrying out of the provisions thereof, including the making of any financial adjustment required to be made for that purpose and the crediting or charging of the amount of any such adjustment to the appropriate account or accounts established under that plan.
@ref Act s 107(4) (src:2776-2777)
GIVEN province IS A Province
      `the government of the province has requested the Government of Canada to enter into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor in Council approves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a law of the other country makes provision for the payment of old age or other benefits, including survivors' or disability benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial plan makes provision for entering into such an agreement and carrying out its provisions, including any financial adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107(4) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the other country about the provincial pension plan` province `the government of the province has requested the Government of Canada to enter into the agreement` `the Governor in Council approves` `a law of the other country makes provision for the payment of old age or other benefits, including survivors' or disability benefits` `the provincial plan makes provision for entering into such an agreement and carrying out its provisions, including any financial adjustment` MEANS
        province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
    AND `the government of the province has requested the Government of Canada to enter into the agreement`
    AND `the Governor in Council approves`
    AND `a law of the other country makes provision for the payment of old age or other benefits, including survivors' or disability benefits`
    AND `the provincial plan makes provision for entering into such an agreement and carrying out its provisions, including any financial adjustment`
